      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/williston_ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1928 Pastor Max Schleicher founded the Luther Home of Mercy on a 25‑acre cornfield, pioneering care for people with developmental disabilities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/williston_ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Otto Schimming built a Sohio gas station on Main Street in 1930, later becoming a bulk filling station run by Terry Witt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/williston_ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Williston lies about 10 miles south of Lake Erie, where lake‑effect snow can add up to 35 inches each winter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/williston_ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The area’s Mollisols, formed from glacial till, make it a top producer of corn and soybeans.",
